@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/fa-carousel/api"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Carousel: API" ComponentName="FaCarousel&lt;TItem&gt;" DocSlug="fa-carousel" />

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/fa-carousel" />

<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>Items</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;TItem&gt;?</code></td><td>an already-in-memory list. Exactly one of <code>Items</code>/<code>ItemsProvider</code> must be set, or <code>OnParametersSet</code> throws <code>ArgumentException</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ItemsProvider</code></td><td><code>Func&lt;Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;TItem&gt;&gt;&gt;?</code></td><td>fetched once, asynchronously, on first render — no paging to re-fetch on, unlike <code>FaGrid</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ItemTemplate</code></td><td><code>RenderFragment&lt;TItem&gt;</code></td><td>required — each slide's markup</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ShowArrows</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>default <code>true</code>; hidden when there's 1 or fewer slides regardless</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ShowDots</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>default <code>true</code>; hidden when there's 1 or fewer slides regardless</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>AutoPlay</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>default <code>false</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>AutoPlayIntervalMs</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>default <code>4000</code>; ignored unless <code>AutoPlay</code> is set</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>
    No <code>AdditionalAttributes</code> splat on this component — every
    attribute you set is one of the above. For hand-authored slides not backed
    by a real data object, use <code>IReadOnlyList&lt;RenderFragment&gt;</code>
    as <code>TItem</code> with <code>ItemTemplate="frag =&gt; frag"</code>.
</p>
